<title>FRANCE: French '96 non-hospital health spending up 2.3 pct.</title>
<headline>French '96 non-hospital health spending up 2.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>December French spending on non-hospital healthcare fell 0.3 percent, leaving the overall rise in 1996 at 2.3 percent, national health insurance fund Caisse Nationale d'Assurance Maladie (CNAM) said.</p>
<p>The 1996 increase was above the government's target. It has said it had aimed to limit the rise in non-hospital spending to 2.1 percent in 1996 to curb public deficits in preparation for European monetary union.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
